From 23972c2d878cb7d37b562d36e6b8d116bae726ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:35:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): write G49 before the program-end retract when
 G43.4 is active

A section that tilts and then stands upright again ends with no rotary
held off zero. uprightAtEnd() then writes nothing, and onClose wrote
G91 G28 Z0 while G43.4 was still active. A reference return is not
permitted in G43.4 mode (FANUC 30i B-63944EN/02), so the control alarms.

The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now remember in endPreamble that the
last section left G43.4 on (tcpmLeft). onClose writes G49 before its
own retract in that case. The other exits (a held rotary, a trailing
Go home, the next preamble) already write G49 and are unchanged.

The recorded golden fanuc/rotary.nc (a tilted section that ends at
A0 B0) recorded the defect. It gains one G49 line after M5.

Pinned by program_end::fanuc_cancels_tcpm_before_program_end_after_a_tilt_back_to_zero
and program_end::doosan_cancels_tcpm_before_program_end_after_a_tilt_back_to_zero
(upright_after_tilt), and by script_fanuc rotary.

Fixes #4348

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
